 "10214": {
  "en": [
   "Not mother, not daughter, not bride, O beautiful, ravishing one — Urvashi, dweller in paradise.",
   "When evening descends on the cattle-fold, drawing its golden veil over a weary body,",
   "you light the evening lamp in no corner of any house.",
   "With steps entangled in hesitation, trembling breast and downcast eyes,",
   "you do not walk softly smiling to the shy bridal bed at midnight.",
   "Unveiled like the rising dawn, you are unabashed.",
   "When you dance in the gods' court, exulting in rapture,",
   "O rippling, undulant Urvashi,",
   "the hosts of waves in the ocean rise dancing to your rhythm,",
   "the earth's mantle shivers and trembles through the heads of grain,",
   "the blind wind carries your heady fragrance to the four quarters,",
   "like a honey-drunk bee the enchanted poet wanders with craving heart, in unbridled song.",
   "You move with murmuring anklets, veil astream, restless as lightning."
  ],
